From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: keep the chosen passthrough device when it plays
 the stream

On S5 and later, each new stream goes to the first device of the chosen
one's type that supports it, so that TrueHD and DTS-HD MA, which only the
AML card's surround71 carries, reach it rather than hdmi. The search also
replaces a chosen device that supports the stream itself: an ALSA loopback
that is offered TrueHD (binaural decodes it on the box) is passed over for
the AML card, which comes first in the list.

Look further only when the chosen device cannot play the stream. With the
AML card chosen, hdmi does not list TrueHD, so the search runs as before.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp
@@ -3017,11 +3017,13 @@
   m_settings.device = settings->GetString(CSettings::SETTING_AUDIOOUTPUT_AUDIODEVICE);
   m_settings.passthroughdevice = settings->GetString(CSettings::SETTING_AUDIOOUTPUT_PASSTHROUGHDEVICE);
 
-  // find on NEWSTREAM the matching passthrough device by device type
+  // find on NEWSTREAM the matching passthrough device by device type,
+  // unless the chosen one plays the stream itself
   if (format != NULL && (soc_id >= AML_S5 || soc_id == AML_T7))
   {
     std::string device(m_settings.passthroughdevice);
-    if (SupportsFormat(*format, &device))
+    if (!m_sink.SupportsFormat(m_settings.passthroughdevice, *format) &&
+        SupportsFormat(*format, &device))
     {
       if (device != m_settings.passthroughdevice)
       {
